Exercise 2: recycling_checker()



Inputs:


x1 and x2: two numeric vectors



Function purpose: Print a helpful message to the user warning them if dangerous vector recycling will happen when they try to combine the two vectors with some arithmetic operation.

If the vectors are not of the same length, provide informational text. See examples below for how to format this text.

Example 1: x1 is length 4 and x2 is length 2. Informational text: “x1 and x2 are not the same length. To match the length of x1, x2 will be repeated 2 times. You will not get a warning when you combine these two vectors, but just be wary that vector recycling is occurring.”
Example 2: x1 is length 3 and x2 is length 11. Informational text: “x1 and x2 are not the same length. To match the length of x2, x1 will be repeated 3 times fully with the first 2 elements repeated again. You will get a warning when you combine these two vectors.”






Code# Write your function here

recycling_checker &lt;- function(x1, x2) {
  len1 &lt;- length(x1)
  len2 &lt;- length(x2)

  if (len1 == len2) {
    message("x1 and x2 are the same length. No recycling will occur.")
    return(invisible(NULL))
  }

  if (len1 &gt; len2) {
    longer &lt;- "x1"; shorter &lt;- "x2"
    len_larger &lt;- len1; len_smaller &lt;- len2
  } else {
    longer &lt;- "x2"; shorter &lt;-"x1"
    len_larger &lt;- len2; len_smaller &lt;- len1
  }

  times_full &lt;- len_larger %/% len_smaller
  remainder  &lt;- len_larger %%  len_smaller

  if (remainder == 0) {
    message(str_glue(
      "x1 and x2 are not the same length. To match the length of {longer}, ",
      "{shorter} will be repeated {times_full} times. ",
      "You will not get a warning when you combine these two vectors, ",
      "but just be wary that vector recycling is occurring."
    ))
  } else {
    message(str_glue(
      "x1 and x2 are not the same length. To match the length of {longer}, ",
      "{shorter} will be repeated {times_full} times fully with the first ",
      "{remainder} element{if (remainder == 1) '' else 's'} repeated again. ",
      "You will get a warning when you combine these two vectors."
    ))
  }
}

# Test cases
recycling_checker(1:4, 1:2)
recycling_checker(1:3, 1:11)
recycling_checker(1:6, 1:4)
recycling_checker(1:2, 1:8)
recycling_checker(1:5, 1:5)

Ex 1
Write a function called get_acs1() that gets 1-year ACS data for a given year for a set of user specified variables for all states. Function arguments should include: - year: Within your function check that this is between 2005 and 2022 and not 2020 (data only available from 2005-2022 except for 2020). If the year is outside this range, include stop("Helpful error message here") to display a helpful error message to the user. - variables: A character vector of variable names to obtain. e.g., c("B02015_009", "B01003_001"). Note that these don’t have “E” or “M” at the end. You’ll always return the “E” version (for the estimate). See next argument for the “M” version. Make sure your function can also handle variables like NAME. - include_moe: TRUE/FALSE indicator of whether to additionally include the “M” version (for the margin of error on the estimate). Set the default to TRUE. - key: Census API key (if you have trouble getting a key, email the instructor as soon as possible) Your function should include a Sys.sleep(0.5) at the beginning to pause code execution for 0.5 seconds. While the Census API does not seem to have a rate limit when you provide an API key, include this pause just to be safe.

Codelibrary(tidyverse)
library(httr)
library(jsonlite)

get_acs1 &lt;- function(year, variables, include_moe = TRUE, key) {
  Sys.sleep(0.5)

  if (!year %in% c(2005:2019, 2021:2022)) {
    stop("Year must be between 2005 and 2022, excluding 2020.")
  }
  name_var&lt;- variables[variables == "NAME"]
  coded_vars&lt;- variables[variables != "NAME"]

  get_parts &lt;- c(name_var, if (length(coded_vars) &gt; 0) paste0(coded_vars, "E"),
                 if (include_moe && length(coded_vars) &gt; 0) paste0(coded_vars, "M")
                 )
  get_string &lt;- paste(get_parts, collapse = ",")

  url&lt;-paste0(
    "https://api.census.gov/data/", year,
    "/acs/acs1?get=", get_string,
    "&for=state:*",
    "&key=", key
  )
  response &lt;- GET(url)

  if (status_code(response) != 200) {
    stop("API request failed with status: ",status_code(response))
  }
  raw &lt;- content(response, as="text", encoding="UTF-8")
  parsed&lt;- fromJSON(raw)

  df &lt;- as.data.frame(parsed[-1, ],stringsAsFactors=FALSE)
  colnames(df) &lt;- parsed[1, ]
  df &lt;- df |&gt; mutate(year = year)

  return(df)
}

